  (history ("claude" "2026-10-11" "Cloudstair SOUND (Opus take): S, Above the Cloud, first visit. The lift's air rushes and thins while sun bells climb out of the cloud (D A E, the open fifth and ninth); then a high flute sings over a bright pad in 3/4, D Mixolydian with the third held back: Dsus2, C/D, G/D, C, Am7, G, C, Dsus4, C, D. Its second phrase climbs to C6, the flat seventh, at the top of the sky, and it lands on an open D: the F# that would complete the chord is H5's note, still ahead at V, so no F# sounds anywhere. Seed-harp plucks catch the light on each beat. A silent 6 s pattern lets it ring out."))))
